What is GM Food Safety Testing?
GM Food Safety Testing encompasses analytical techniques used to detect, identify, and quantify genetically modified organisms (GMOs) in agricultural commodities, food ingredients, and processed food products. Testing methods such as polymerase chain reaction (PCR), quantitative PCR (qPCR), enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA), digital PCR, and next-generation sequencing (NGS) enable manufacturers, laboratories, and regulators to verify GMO content, support labeling compliance, and maintain traceability throughout the food supply chain.
